    {
      "@id": "#specimen-imaging-preparation-protocol-idr0113-bottes-opcclones-experimenta",
      "@type": "bia:SpecimenImagingPreparationProtocol",
      "name": "Specimen imaging preparation protocol",
      "description": "The surgical intervention for demyelinating an area of the CC and placing the transcortical window was carried out in Ascl1CreERT2/tdTom mice aged ok 9- 12 weeks. A stereotaxic injection of 2 _l of a solution of 1% lysolecithin (LPc) in 0.9% NaCl was performed in deeply anaesthetized mice. LPC was injected unilaterally into the CC at -1.3 mm dorso/ventral from brain surface and -2.5 12 mm anterior/posterior, -0.9mm lateral from Bregma. After 30 minutes, the implantation of the window was started. above the demyelinated CC (-2.5 anterior/posterior / Đ1.5 mediolateral mm from Bregma) the cranial bone is locally removed (circle 3mm Ż). A cylinder (3mm Ż) of cortical tissue that has been punched out using biopsy punches until a defined depth (1.5mm deep from skull, level of the corpus callosum) was aspirated using a blunt needle (22g) connected to an air pump until white matter tracks were visible. The area was cleaned and the window (3mm Ż stainless steel cannula, 1.5mm height, covered by a 3mm Ż glass coverslip) was inserted, secured in place using the stereotactic arm and stably fixed to the cranial bone with UV curable dental cement.\"\n\n\"Two and three days after surgery, sparse labeling of OPCs was achieved by i.p. injection of Tamoxifen (Tam; 180mg/kg bodyweight). Imaging fields of view containing identified OPCs were selected to obtain 10-20 SPOTs per mouse. Chronic 2-photon imaging was performed starting 3 days after surgery. All SPOTs were checked on a daily basis and no z-stack was acquired if no changes occurred. The imaging was performed on custom-built 2-photon microscope (Sutter Instrument Movable Objective Microscope type) using a long-working distance objective (water immersion, 16x magnification, 0.8NA, Nikon) and equipped with a ytterbium-doped laser system at 1045nm and 200fs (Femtotrain, High-Q lasers) or a fiber oscillator 45 laser at 1070nm (Fidelity-2, Coherent) to excite tdTomato labeled cells in the CC. Emission light was detected using a photomultiplier tube (Hamamatsu) after passing a red emission filter (610/75 nm; AHF).\n\nEvery cell of each lineage was annotated with a code. The coding parameters were: Cell ID, Cell Type, Uncertainty Cell Type, Time point, Mother ID, Uncertainty Mother Cell, Sister ID, Uncertainty Sister Cell and Cell Death. For details see document \"\"ROIs code explanation\"\"."
    },
